architecture-section.content:

**Game State:**
```typescript
interface GameState {
  // Current evening state
  coziness: number;           // 0-100
  timeRemaining: number;      // seconds
  score: number;              // points
  activeEvents: GameEvent[];  // currently active events

  // Game status
  isPlaying: boolean;
  isPaused: boolean;
  gameOver: boolean;
}
```

**Timer Access:**
- Timer reads from `GameContext.gameState.timeRemaining`
- timeRemaining is a number (seconds)
- Timer updates automatically when GameContext updates (React re-render)

**GameContext Usage:** ```typescript // In Timer component: import { useGame } from '../contexts/GameContext';
const { gameState } = useGame(); const timeRemaining = gameState.timeRemaining; // number in seconds ```
**State Updates:** - Timer value updated in game loop (useGameLoop.ts) - setTimeRemaining called every frame (frame-rate independent) - Component re-renders automatically when timeRemaining changes - No local state needed if reading directly from context
